# E §3.1 step 1 and L §8.3 (tally 2.1.3, issue #60): `reprint` names a loose file as `run` does, as given, so two files
# with one base name, a/x.tally and b/x.tally, print under their two paths, in full-path order. Was two sections named
# `--- x.tally` (T's SR-4: 10 of the suite's sets); the order and the hash were already these.
=== options disk reprint
=== b/x.tally
part p
  tally 2

input z: int
=== a/x.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
